    Bind the norm parameter tables into the norm plan
    
    The norm plan can carry the gain and bias parameter table identities: the plan
    validates the tables plan, requires both parameter widths to equal the padded
    column domain, absorbs the tables digest into the plan digest and bumps the
    bind version. The digest of each identity now encodes the committed reader
    (root, configuration, shape numbers, distances and the record) inline, so the
    plan digest binds the whole table identity without a separate fallible step. A
    plan test checks the digest change, the width binding, the kind swap and the
    duplicate row rejection.
    
    partial progress

